To the Public Records Advocate / Attorney General's Office:<br>
<br>
I petition, under ORS 192.411, for review of the Oregon Department of Admin=
istrative Services' response to public records request R000879-070126, subm=
itted July 1, 2026.<br>
<br>
The request sought the Department's own records concerning me =97 its commu=
nications referencing me with the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department, t=
he Office of the Governor, and any other state entity, and records naming o=
r identifiably describing me. The
 Department first closed it on the ground that it &quot;is not the custodia=
n,&quot; referring me to OPRD. After reopening, it closed the request a sec=
ond time, on July 27, 2026, determining &quot;no responsive records&quot; a=
s to both categories while again referring me to OPRD.
 It has never described the search behind either determination, never subst=
antiated or withdrawn the custodial determination, cited no exemption, and =
never acknowledged the July 7, 2026 preservation notice.<br>
<br>
The attached petition asks the Attorney General to order the Department to =
do what ORS 192.329 requires: to produce, cite a specific exemption, or sta=
te expressly that no responsive record exists; to describe the search =97 i=
ncluding whether it reached the Department's
 communications with state entities other than OPRD; to either identify the=
 public body for which it claims to have acted as an agent under ORS 192.31=
1(2)(b) or withdraw the custodial referral; to state whether the preservati=
on notice was received and distributed;
 and to impose the penalty available under ORS 192.407 for undue delay.<br>
<br>
The petition and its eighteen exhibits are attached.<br>
<br>
Respectfully,<br>
Robert Samuel White<br>
P.O. Box 334, Reedsport, Oregon 97467<br>
rsw@rswfire.com =97 458-230-1869</div>
